      "side": 1,
      "message": "Empty Cc now reaches the SMTP envelope as an invalid recipient. With cc\u003d[] (the jira_watchers value, and any deployment with an empty/blank report_cc since build_cc_users returns []), `\",\".join(cc)` sets an empty `Cc:` header. smtplib\u0027s send_message only skips headers that are None (`addr_fields \u003d [f for f in (msg[\u0027To\u0027], msg[\u0027Bcc\u0027], msg[\u0027Cc\u0027]) if f is not None]`); an empty string is included and `getaddresses([... , \u0027\u0027])` yields (\u0027\u0027, \u0027\u0027)`, so to_addrs gets \u0027\u0027 and the session issues `RCPT TO:\u003c\u003e`.\n\nVerified live with the real plugin against a local SMTP sink (cc\u003d[]): `mail from:\u003cquads@example.com\u003e` / `rcpt to:\u003cdwilson@example.com\u003e` / `rcpt to:\u003c\u003e` / `data`. Note the previous bspreston-esq review note: sendmail only raises SMTPRecipientsRefused when ALL recipients are refused, so a 501/553 on `\u003c\u003e` is tolerated (delivery still succeeds) — but a mail server that answers 421 or resets on the malformed RCPT makes the whole send fail (`close(); raise SMTPRecipientsRefused`), so send_mail returns False and the notification is silently lost; the payload also carries an empty `Cc:` header.\n\nSuggest: only set the header when non-empty — `if cc: msg[\"Cc\"] \u003d \",\".join(cc)` (and the same treatment for To) — and add a regression test with cc\u003d[] asserting no empty header and no \u0027\u0027 in the envelope; the current test only exercises a 2-entry Cc. jira_watchers.py:96 (cc\u003d[]) hits this on every failed-watchers email, i.e. exactly the path that should reliably reach the To recipient.",
      "revId": "c63e220b1a00a024dfff8453befead1b254309f6",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
