      "writtenOn": "2026-09-29T17:48:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sanitization currently lives only at the notify*/validator call sites, not at the plugin boundary. Now that send_message derives the envelope from the headers, this line trusts whatever `cc` a caller hands the dispatcher: `cc\u003dNone` breaks `compose` (`\",\".join(None)` → TypeError → send_mail returns False with \"Unexpected error\", and the dispatcher\u0027s own signature is `cc: Optional[List[str]] \u003d None`), and a bare username lands as `RCPT TO:\u003cbob\u003e` (getaddresses: (\u0027\u0027, \u0027bob\u0027)). build_cc_users is the right centralization for the notify family, but the EmailPlugin interface remains the choke point every future caller goes through. Suggest normalizing defensively here: `cc \u003d cc or []` and qualify/drop non-address entries (or at least `if cc:`) so the envelope is only ever built from parseable addresses.",
      "revId": "c63e220b1a00a024dfff8453befead1b254309f6",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
